As far as the convergence and error bounds are concerned, (3.41) implies that

\[|\mathbf{u}_{h}(\lambda)-\mathbf{u}(\lambda)|_{1,\,\Omega}+|\lambda|\,\|p_{h}( \lambda)-p(\lambda)\|_{0,\,\Omega}\leqslant K\,\|(T_{h}-\,T)G(\lambda,u(\lambda) )\|_{X}.\]

Hence (4.6) follows from (4.9). Furthermore, since

\[u(\lambda)=(\mathbf{u}(\lambda),\lambda p(\lambda))\,\in H^{m+1}(\Omega)^{N} \times H^{m}(\Omega)\]

is the solution of the Stokes system:

\[u(\lambda)=-\,TG(\lambda,u(\lambda)),\]

the error estimate (II.1.46) gives:

\[\|(T_{h}-\,T)G(\lambda,u(\lambda))\|_{X}\leqslant Ch^{m}\{\,\|\mathbf{u}( \lambda)\|_{m+1,\,\Omega}+\,\|p(\lambda)\|_{m,\,\Omega}\}.\]

Thus (4.7) stems from the continuity of the mapping \(\lambda\to u(\lambda)\) from \(\Lambda\) into \(H^{m+1}(\Omega)^{N}\times H^{m}(\Omega)\). 

It is also possible to derive an \(L^{2}\)-estimate for the velocity. Like in the linear case we must assume that the associated Stokes problem is _regular_ (cf. Definition II.1.1):

(4.11) \[\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\text{the mapping }(\phi,\mu)\to-\,v\,\lambda\phi+ \mathbf{grad}\,\mu\text{ is an isomorphism from }[H^{2}(\Omega)^{N}\cap V]\times[H^{1}(\Omega)\cap L^{2}_{0}(\Omega)]\text{ onto }L^{2}(\Omega)^{N}.\end{array}\right.\]

**Theorem 4.2**.: _We retain the hypotheses of Theorem 4.1 and we assume that (4.11) holds. If the mapping \(\lambda\to(\mathbf{u}(\lambda),p(\lambda))\) is continuous from \(\Lambda\) into \(H^{m+1}(\Omega)^{N}\times H^{m}(\Omega)\) for some integer \(m\) in \([1,l],\) then we have the following \(L^{2}\)-estimate for all \(\lambda\) in \(\Lambda\):_

(4.12) \[\|\mathbf{u}_{h}(\lambda)-\mathbf{u}(\lambda)\|_{0,\,\Omega}\leqslant Kh^{m+1}.\]

Proof.: Let us apply Theorem 3.5. Since we are only interested in the velocity \(\mathbf{u}\), we are going to drop entirely the pressure \(p\). Thus we take

\[X=H^{1}_{0}(\Omega)^{N},\ \ \ \ \ Y=H^{-1}(\Omega)^{N}\]

and for \(\mathbf{f}\) in \(Y\) we define \(\mathbf{v}=\,T\mathbf{f}\) by:

\[\mathbf{v}\,\in\,V,\ \ \ \ (\mathbf{grad}\,\mathbf{v},\mathbf{grad}\,\mathbf{w})= \langle\mathbf{f},\mathbf{w}\rangle\ \ \ \ \ \forall\mathbf{w}\,\in\,V.\]

As the mapping \(G(\lambda,v)\) depends only on the velocity \(\mathbf{v}\) (and not on \(q\)) we can leave it as such. Thus, \(\mathbf{u}\) is a solution of the Navier-Stokes system (4.1) if and only if:

\[F(\lambda,\mathbf{u})\equiv\mathbf{u}\,+\,TG(\lambda,\mathbf{u})=\mathbf{0}.\]

Next, we choose

\[H=L^{2}(\Omega)^{N},\ \ \ \ W=[H^{1}_{0}(\Omega)\cap H^{2}(\Omega)]^{N}.\]

From Theorem I.1.3, we know that \(X\) (resp. \(W\)) is compactly imbedded into \(H\) (resp. \(X\)). Now, take \(\mathbf{u}\) in \(W\) and let us check that \(D_{u}G(\lambda,\mathbf{u})\,\in\,\mathcal{L}(H;\,Y)=\,\mathcal{L}(L^{2}(\Omega )^{N};H^{\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,
